# `todo/t1373` / `todo/t1319` — RECEIVER PLACE: PLAIN PARAMETER.
#
# The plainest shape in the language: pass a `Box` to a function and read it.
# `resolve_param_type` binds the parameter as `Ptr(Box__T)`, the D31 default is
# borrow, and the by-value `Box__T__get` then read the parameter SLOT's address
# as the handle.
#
# ⚠ `plain_param` IS NOT IN `opaque_handle_route_fixtures_exist`'s ROUTES list
# (`todo/t1471`), so nothing else in the tree holds this cell.
#
# RED-VERIFIED AS WRITTEN against the pre-fix compiler: garbage on C, `41` on
# LLVM. POST-fix: `41` on both.
#
# ⚠ ONE RECEIVER PLACE PER FILE, AND THAT IS A MEASUREMENT, NOT A STYLE RULE.
# `ensure_extern` (src/lir/lower/operands.rs) synthesizes ONE declaration per
# MANGLED SYMBOL from whichever call site is lowered first, so five places
# sharing one payload emit exactly ONE `Box__int64_t__get` and all five sites
# marshal against it: the file would claim five cells in its NAME and pin one.
# Splitting by payload does not rescue it either — `Box[int]` and `Box[int64]`
# collapse to the SAME symbol. And the order that decides the winner is
# LOWERING order, not statement order: top-level function bodies lower before
# `main`, so a file that reads its control first is not thereby safe.
#
# ⚠ LIVES IN `tests/fixtures/self_host_gaps/`, NOT AT TOP LEVEL. Every
# top-level `tests/fixtures/*.gg` is auto-scanned into `runtime_parity_corpus`;
# the self-host lane has NO `is_by_value_receiver` chokepoint to mirror this
# fix into (`todo/t1537`), so a top-level landing would push
# `RUNTIME_DIFF_NONMATCH_CEILING` past a shrink-only pin that sits at zero
# slack — and Core #9 ⊕ forbids raising it for a round's own inflow. The
# Rust-lane coverage is unchanged (`run_gg` runs it like any fixture).
# Graduating these to top level is what closes `todo/t1537`.

int peek(Box[int] b):
    return b.get()

void main():
    Box[int] bb = Box(41)
    print(peek(bb))
